+## At the entrance display
+
+When you check in at a door configured to welcome members on this kiosk, or tap your fob on the reader beside the display, WelcomePi greets you with your first name in large letters. If the door sends your name first, the display shows it immediately. Once the kiosk receives your fob’s card ID for the check-in and verifies your membership, the kiosk adds “Member through” and your expiration date below your name. Your agenda opens automatically when it has data to show (or finishes loading an empty agenda) and the large welcome has been visible for at least three seconds. If only your name appears, tap your active fob on the kiosk reader to open your agenda. The door reader records your arrival. A local tap controls the display. The kiosk logs the member name and reader location for recognized scans.
+
+**Your reservations** covers the next 12 hours, including time already underway. Pending and unpaid reservations carry a label. **Volunteer opportunities** shows work you can claim worth at least the configured minimum (one point by default). Tasks restricted to today's weekday get the first two places when available. Space permitting, the screen also shows today's Eventbrite classes and a QR code for the portal Home page.
+
+**Everyone near the screen can see your personal information if you open it.** While your agenda is on screen, tap your own active fob on the kiosk reader to open your details. Ledger participants see their character sheet and current avatar or rank icon. Other members see the text of kudos they have received, including private messages, followed by their current tool checkouts. Tap once more to clear your details.
+
+A different local fob starts its owner's welcome immediately. On the details screen you have 30 seconds before a waiting arrival with a verified fob takes over. A name-only arrival leaves your details on screen. After two minutes without a qualifying scan, the display returns to the five most recently checked-in members from the past 16 hours, lifetime volunteer point leaders, available work, and the portal QR code. Each member appears once at their latest arrival time, including arrivals at doors that do not open a welcome on this kiosk. After four hours it sleeps until the next qualifying scan.
+
+The public board changes colors and moves the portal QR through all four corners to reduce monitor burn-in. The QR can extend past the colored title bar into a clear corner. It stays steady as the lists page, so you can keep your phone aimed at it. A fresh door check-in or a tap on the display's reader brightens a dim board. Greetings, agendas and details stay at normal brightness and use a different layout the next time you open them.
+
 ## For admins

 Admins can open the tab on a member's profile. For admins it also lists **Additional Details** for each scan, such as the **Card Holder**, plus the validity and location. Use it to help a member whose fob does not work: find their recent scans and read the validity of the refused ones. Open it only for a real need, such as a member asking for help, and do not share what you see with others.
